Litmus tests for fully ordered powerpc atomics
==============================================

LKMM C tests (herd7 -conf tools/memory-model/linux-kernel.cfg):

  SB+atomicincmb+atomicincmb.litmus
	Never. Store buffering forbidden when each side uses
	atomic_inc_return() on a *different* counter as the fence.

  SB+atomicincrel+atomicincacq.litmus
	Sometimes. Contrast: release RMW + acquire RMW on independent
	counters is not a full barrier.

  MP+atomicincmb.litmus
	Never. Message passing through fully ordered RMWs.

PPC ISA tests (herd7, first line "PPC ..."):

  SB+lwsyncs.litmus
	Sometimes. lwsync does not order store-load.

  SB+syncs.litmus
	Never. Two hwsyncs (the old mapping).

  SB+lwsync-lwarx-stwcx-isync.litmus
	Sometimes in herd's Power model (only sync is a strong fence;
	stcx completion is not in ppc.cat). Not a disproof of the ISA
	mapping. Controls: SB+lwsyncs Sometimes, SB+syncs Never.

Run:

  ./run-litmus.sh

Requires herd7 from https://github.com/herd/herdtools7
If herd7 is missing the script skips (exit 4).
